{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-06-06T22:48:40.613Z","evidence":{"seeds":"trellis-6eb1","commit":"17bed8f6372b6a35ee8db4fc57527577e643f86c"},"relates_to":["mx-7a0d74"],"dir_anchors":["src/report"],"title":"Fleet = targets.yaml loader + sequential orchestration over the same audit core","rationale":"trellis-6eb1 builds src/fleet/ as three modules + barrel: targets.ts (strict zod schema + loadFleet, path-resolution relative to the targets.yaml dir, duplicate-id guard, TargetsError) and the pure targetAuditOptions() WHAT→audit seam mapping a ResolvedTarget+defaults onto AuditOptions; orchestrate.ts runFleet() audits each target sequentially via the SAME core auditRepo (audit+drift), persists each run, and computes a level delta by reading store.latestRun(id) BEFORE insertRun; report.ts renders terminal/md (json is the FleetReport itself). Per-target failures (missing path, audit throw) isolate into ok:false entries — the fleet never aborts. To make this work, auditRepo gained repoId (stamps report.repo + drift.repo + cache key so central state keys on the targets.yaml id, not basename), skip (forces criteria not-applicable with rationale SKIPPED_VIA_TARGETS), and osecoDetectors (plumbed onto DetectionContext, default-on, forward-compat for trellis-7f70); driftRepo gained repoId. defaults.investigation maps to investigateOpts.targetDefaults. Orchestrator takes injectable store/audit/pathExists/now for offline determinism. auditRepo was refactored (scoreAllCriteria + foldDrift + deterministicEntry helpers) to stay under the cognitive-complexity ratchet after the additions.","id":"mx-592b8d","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-09-19T16:07:00.211Z","archive_reason":"manual: Superseded by the current deterministic audit architecture and source cleanup; see SPEC.md and AGENTS.md."}
