{"type":"decision","classification":"tactical","recorded_at":"2026-09-17T02:22:53.509Z","evidence":{"seeds":"trellis-8366","commit":"5056467f7dfb53db02a68b08520e9bac0f729f54"},"dir_anchors":["src/cli","src/fleet","src/history"],"title":"Fleet adapts to the deterministic core by folding runWorkspaceAudit per target (trellis-8366)","rationale":"Post-pivot fleet (SPEC §11) has no fleet-level scoring: each targets.yaml target runs the same runWorkspaceAudit service the CLI/SDK fold, and the FleetReport entry embeds the full §6.4 report + the target's own declarative §9 PolicyAssessment, so fleet results are deep-equal to independent core audits by construction. Canonical drift rides along per target via targetDriftOptions as a separate non-scoring capability (driftError isolated, never gates); fleet runs are stateless by default with --history opting into persistence + baseline index deltas. Legacy targets keys (skip, languages, defaults.investigation) are accepted by the zod schema only so loadFleet can reject them with actionable migration messages — the accept-then-reject pattern already used for defaults.investigation.","id":"mx-64df1b","status":"archived","archived_at":"2026-09-19T16:07:00.211Z","archive_reason":"manual: Superseded by the current deterministic audit architecture and source cleanup; see SPEC.md and AGENTS.md."}
